    Fix response-shape mismatches causing blank pages on Chat/Documents tabs
    
    This app has no React Error Boundary anywhere, so an uncaught
    render-time exception in any component crashes the entire React
    tree, not just that tab -- explaining why both Chat and Documents
    appeared blank together from a single root cause.
    
    DocumentUpload.js: GET /api/document/my-documents actually returns
    { success: true, documents: [...] } (confirmed by reading
    DocumentController.cs), but the component did
    setDocuments(response.data), storing the whole wrapped object as
    state. The render then calls documents.map(...), which throws
    "documents.map is not a function" on that object -- an uncaught
    render error that unmounts the whole app. Fixed to unwrap
    response.data.documents.
    
    Chat.js: POST /api/chat/search-local actually returns
    { hasResults, context, message } (a single text block, confirmed by
    reading ChatController.cs's SearchLocalDatabase action), not
    { chunks: [...] } as the component assumed. This didn't crash
    (localResults.chunks && ... short-circuited safely) but silently
    showed "No relevant documents found" even when the backend did find
    something. Fixed handleAcceptLocalResults and the results render to
    use hasResults/context directly instead of a nonexistent chunks
    array.
    
    Both mismatches trace back to the frontend being recreated from
    scratch earlier this session (the original Frontend/ directory was
    lost when a git submodule reference was removed) without direct
    visibility into the real backend response shapes at the time.
    
    Verified locally: npm run build compiles successfully with these
    changes.
    
    Note: also found the Tests tab's api.js calls (POST /api/test/run,
    GET /api/test/results) don't match any actual TestController route
    (GET /api/test/run-section-e, GET /api/test/run-all exist instead).
    Left unfixed since it wasn't reported as broken and is a properly
    caught error, not a crash -- flagging for a separate fix if wanted.
    
